Context of the rv32 run
The configuration under which the translator ran, and every
interpretation that a model of the run uses. The Interpretations
section of backend/README.md explains each interpretation; a comment
at the top of a model lists what is specific to it.

Configuration
  extension Ext_Zca=off
  extension Ext_Zicfilp=off

Interpretations
  Each Sail call or construct is replaced by the HOL term below it. a,
  b, ... stand for its arguments, s for the state before it, s' for the
  state after it and s0 for the state at the start of the instruction.

  PC
    ~> riscv_instruction_pc s0
  cur_privilege
    ~> read reg_cur_5fprivilege s
  currentlyEnabled(Ext_Zca)
    ~> F
  currentlyEnabled(Ext_Zicfilp)
    ~> F
  exception_context(a, b)
    ~> (a,b)
  generate_event(EV_FENCE)
    ~> one
  get_arch_pc()
    ~> riscv_instruction_pc s0
  get_next_pc()
    ~> read PC s
  is_fiom_active()
    ~> read reg_is_5ffiom_5factive s
  rX_bits(a)
    ~> read (riscv_gpr a) s
  return Retire_Success()
    ~> the final state is write events
      (CONS (EventJump ((riscv_instruction_pc s0),(read PC s)))
      (read events s)) s
  sail_barrier(Barrier_RISCV_r_r)
    ~> one
  sail_barrier(Barrier_RISCV_r_rw)
    ~> one
  sail_barrier(Barrier_RISCV_r_w)
    ~> one
  sail_barrier(Barrier_RISCV_rw_r)
    ~> one
  sail_barrier(Barrier_RISCV_rw_rw)
    ~> one
  sail_barrier(Barrier_RISCV_rw_w)
    ~> one
  sail_barrier(Barrier_RISCV_tso)
    ~> one
  sail_barrier(Barrier_RISCV_w_r)
    ~> one
  sail_barrier(Barrier_RISCV_w_rw)
    ~> one
  sail_barrier(Barrier_RISCV_w_w)
    ~> one
  set_next_pc(a)
    ~> s' = write PC a s
  trap(a)
    ~> sail_hl_ctor_Trap
  vmem_read(a, b, 1, Load(Data), false, false, false)
    ~> for addr = word_add (read (riscv_gpr a) s) b: if
      ((val addr) MOD 1) = 0
      (a copy of Sail's is_aligned_addr, not its translation) then s' =
      write events (CONS (EventLoad (addr,1)) (read events s)) s,
      returning INL (read (memory :> (bytes8 addr)) s); else every final
      state, in place of Sail's plat_misaligned_exception, whose outcome
      the platform chooses
  vmem_read(a, b, 2, Load(Data), false, false, false)
    ~> for addr = word_add (read (riscv_gpr a) s) b: if
      ((val addr) MOD 2) = 0
      (a copy of Sail's is_aligned_addr, not its translation) then s' =
      write events (CONS (EventLoad (addr,2)) (read events s)) s,
      returning INL (read (memory :> (bytes16 addr)) s); else every
      final state, in place of Sail's plat_misaligned_exception, whose
      outcome the platform chooses
  vmem_read(a, b, 4, Load(Data), false, false, false)
    ~> for addr = word_add (read (riscv_gpr a) s) b: if
      ((val addr) MOD 4) = 0
      (a copy of Sail's is_aligned_addr, not its translation) then s' =
      write events (CONS (EventLoad (addr,4)) (read events s)) s,
      returning INL (read (memory :> (bytes32 addr)) s); else every
      final state, in place of Sail's plat_misaligned_exception, whose
      outcome the platform chooses
  vmem_write(a, b, 1, c, Store(Data), false, false, false)
    ~> for addr = word_add (read (riscv_gpr a) s) b: if
      ((val addr) MOD 1) = 0
      (a copy of Sail's is_aligned_addr, not its translation) then s' =
      write events (CONS (EventStore (addr,1)) (read events s))
      (write (memory :> (bytes8 addr)) c s), returning INL T; else every
      final state, in place of Sail's plat_misaligned_exception, whose
      outcome the platform chooses
  vmem_write(a, b, 2, c, Store(Data), false, false, false)
    ~> for addr = word_add (read (riscv_gpr a) s) b: if
      ((val addr) MOD 2) = 0
      (a copy of Sail's is_aligned_addr, not its translation) then s' =
      write events (CONS (EventStore (addr,2)) (read events s))
      (write (memory :> (bytes16 addr)) c s), returning INL T; else
      every final state, in place of Sail's plat_misaligned_exception,
      whose outcome the platform chooses
  vmem_write(a, b, 4, c, Store(Data), false, false, false)
    ~> for addr = word_add (read (riscv_gpr a) s) b: if
      ((val addr) MOD 4) = 0
      (a copy of Sail's is_aligned_addr, not its translation) then s' =
      write events (CONS (EventStore (addr,4)) (read events s))
      (write (memory :> (bytes32 addr)) c s), returning INL T; else
      every final state, in place of Sail's plat_misaligned_exception,
      whose outcome the platform chooses
  wX_bits(a, b)
    ~> s' = write (riscv_gpr a) b s
